\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\ul\b\f0\fs32\lang9   Flowchat \par
\ulnone\b0\fs22 A flowchart is a graphical representation of a process, system, or algorithm. It helps to visualize the steps in a process using symbols to represent actions, decisions, or data flows.\par
\ul Basic Flowchart Symbols:\par
\ulnone\b Oval\b0 : Represents the Start or End of a process.\par
\b Rectangle\b0 : Represents a Process or action to be performed.\par
\b Diamond\b0 : Represents a Decision point where a Yes/No or True/False choice is made.\par
\b Parallelogram\b0 : Represents Input/Output, like reading data or displaying output.\par
\b Arrow\b0 : Shows the Flow or direction of the process.\par
Example of a Simple Flowchart for Logging Into a System:\par
Start \f1\u8594?\f0  Oval\par
Input Username \f1\u8594?\f0  Parallelogram\par
Input Password \f1\u8594?\f0  Parallelogram\par
Validate Credentials \f1\u8594?\f0  Rectangle\par
Decision: Credentials Correct? \f1\u8594?\f0  Diamond\par
If Yes \f1\u8594?\f0  Proceed to Dashboard \f1\u8594?\f0  Rectangle \f1\u8594?\f0  End (Oval)\par
If No \f1\u8594?\f0  Show Error Message \f1\u8594?\f0  Rectangle \f1\u8594?\f0  Return to Input Username\par
\par
********************************************************************************************\par
\b Overall Execution Flow in Java (Order)\b0\par

