\b\fs32 Variables & Data Types\par
\b0\fs22 Variables\par
A variable is a container (storage area) used to hold data.  it has name,value and type\par
Each variable should be given a unique name (identifier).  \par
public class Main \{\par
   public static void main(String[] args) \{\par
      // Variables\par
       String name = "Aman";\par
       int age = 30;\par
       String neighbour = "Akku";\par
       String friend = neighbour;\par
   \}\par
\}\par
A variable is used to store data\par
It has a name, type, and value\par
Types include:\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Primitive (int, float, etc.)\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Non-primitive (String, arrays, objects)\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Based on scope:\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Local --> Declared inside a method , Accessible only within that method\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Instance --> Declared inside a class but outside methods , Each object has its own copy\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Static --> Declared using static keyword , Shared by all objects\par

