\b\fs32 Conditional Statements \f2\lquote\f0 if-else\b0\f2\rquote\f0\par
\fs22 The if block is used to specify the code to be executed if the condition specified  in if is true, the else block is executed otherwise.\par
\par
int age = 30;\par
if(age > 18) \{\par
   System.out.println("This is an adult");\par
\} else \{\par
   System.out.println("This is not an adult");\par
\}\b\par
\fs32 Conditional Statements \f2\lquote\f0 switch\f2\rquote\f0\par
\b0\fs22 Switch case statements are a substitute for long if statements that compare a\par
variable to multiple values. After a match is found, it executes the\par
corresponding code of that value case.\par
The following example is to print days of the week:\par
\par
int n = 1;\par
switch(n) \{\par
   case 1 :\par
       System.out.println("Monday");\par
       break;\par
   case 2 :\par
       System.out.println("Tuesday");\par
       break;\par
   case 3 :\par
       System.out.println("Wednesday");\par
       break;\par
   case 4 :\par
       System.out.println("Thursday");\par
       break;\par
   case 5:\par
       System.out.println("Friday");\par
       break;\par
   case 6 :\par
       System.out.println("Saturday");\par
       break;\par
   default :\par
       System.out.println("Sunday");\par
\}\par
