\ul\b Homework Problems\par
\ulnone Print the spiral order matrix as output for a given matrix of numbers. [Difficult for Beginners]\par
\b0 APPROACH : \par
Algorithm: (We are given a 2D matrix of n X m ).\par
1. We will need 4 variables:\par
a. row_start - initialized with 0.\par
b. row_end - initialized with n-1.\par
c. column_start - initialized with 0.\par
d. column_end - initialized with m-1.\par
2. First of all, we will traverse in the row row_start from column_start\par
to column_end and we will increase the row_start with 1 as we have\par
traversed the starting row.\par
3. Then we will traverse in the column column_end from row_start to\par
row_end and decrease the column_end by 1.\par
4. Then we will traverse in the row row_end from column_end to\par
column_start and decrease the row_end by 1.\par
5. Then we will traverse in the column column_start from row_end to\par
row_start and increase the column_start by 1.\par
6. We will do the above steps from 2 to 5 until row_start <= row_end\par
and column_start <= column_end.\par
import java.util.*;\par
\par
\par
public class Arrays \{\par
   public static void main(String args[]) \{\par
      Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\par
      int n = sc.nextInt();\par
      int m = sc.nextInt();\par
      int matrix[][] = new int[n][m];\par
      for(int i=0; i<n; i++) \{\par
           for(int j=0; j<m; j++) \{\par
               matrix[i][j] = sc.nextInt();\par
           \}\par
      \}\par
      System.out.println("The Spiral Order Matrix is : ");\par
      int rowStart = 0;\par
      int rowEnd = n-1;\par
      int colStart = 0;\par
      int colEnd = m-1;\par
      //To print spiral order matrix\par
      while(rowStart <= rowEnd && colStart <= colEnd) \{\par
          //1\par
          for(int col=colStart; col<=colEnd; col++) \{\par
              System.out.print(matrix[rowStart][col] + " ");\par
          \}\par
          rowStart++;\par
          //2\par
          for(int row=rowStart; row<=rowEnd; row++) \{\par
              System.out.print(matrix[row][colEnd] +" ");\par
          \}\par
          colEnd--;\par
          //3\par
          for(int col=colEnd; col>=colStart; col--) \{\par
              System.out.print(matrix[rowEnd][col] + " ");\par
          \}\par
          rowEnd--;\par
          //4\par
          for(int row=rowEnd; row>=rowStart; row--) \{\par
              System.out.print(matrix[row][colStart] + " ");\par
          \}\par
          colStart++;\par
          System.out.println();\par
      \}\par
   \}\par
\}\par
