1. StringBuffer\par
\b0 StringBuffer is a mutable sequence of characters that is thread-safe (synchronized).\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\fs20 Mutable (can change content without creating new objects)\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Synchronized \f1\u8594?\f0  safe for multi-threading\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Slightly slower due to synchronization overhead\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Default capacity \f1\u8594?\f0  16\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}With initial string \f1\u8594?\f0  16 + string length\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b\lang1033 2.StringBuilder\b0\par
StringBuilder is also a mutable sequence of characters, but it is not synchronized.\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Mutable\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Not thread-safe\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Faster than StringBuffer\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Recommended for single-threaded environments\par

