\fs22 Bubble Sort\par
\par
\b0 Idea: if arr[i] > arr[i+1] swap them. To place the element in their respective position, we have to do the following operation N-1 times. \par
Time Complexity: O(N2)\par
\par
Code\par
import java.util.*;\par
\par
\par
class Sorting \{\par
   public static void printArray(int arr[]) \{\par
       for(int i=0; i<arr.length; i++) \{\par
           System.out.print(arr[i]+" ");\par
       \}\par
       System.out.println();\par
   \}\par
\par
\par
   public static void main(String args[]) \{\par
       int arr[] = \{7, 8, 1, 3, 2\};\par
\par
\par
       //bubble sort\par
       for(int i=0; i<arr.length-1; i++) \{\par
           for(int j=0; j<arr.length-i-1; j++) \{\par
               if(arr[j] > arr[j+1]) \{\par
                   //swap\par
                   int temp = arr[j];\par
                   arr[j] = arr[j+1];\par
                   arr[j+1] = temp;\par
               \}\par
           \}\par
       \}\par
\par
\par
       printArray(arr);\par
   \}\par
\}\par
\par
\b Selection Sort\par
\par
\b0 Idea: The inner loop selects the minimum element in the unsorted array and places the elements in increasing order. \par
Time complexity: O(N2) \par
\par
Code\par
import java.util.*;\par
\par
\par
class Sorting \{\par
   public static void printArray(int arr[]) \{\par
       for(int i=0; i<arr.length; i++) \{\par
           System.out.print(arr[i]+" ");\par
       \}\par
       System.out.println();\par
   \}\par
\par
\par
   public static void main(String args[]) \{\par
       int arr[] = \{7, 8, 1, 3, 2\};\par
\par
\par
       //selection sort\par
       for(int i=0; i<arr.length-1; i++) \{\par
           int smallest = i;\par
           for(int j=i+1; j<arr.length; j++) \{\par
               if(arr[j] < arr[smallest]) \{\par
                   smallest = j;\par
               \}\par
           \}\par
           //swap\par
           int temp = arr[smallest];\par
           arr[smallest] = arr[i];\par
           arr[i] = temp;\par
       \}\par
\par
\par
       printArray(arr);\par
   \}\par
\}\par
\par
\b Insertion Sort\par
\par
\b0 Idea: Take an element from the unsorted array, place it in its corresponding position in the sorted part, and shift the elements accordingly. \par
Time Complexity: O(N2) \par
\par
Code\par
import java.util.*;\par
\par
\par
class Sorting \{\par
   public static void printArray(int arr[]) \{\par
       for(int i=0; i<arr.length; i++) \{\par
           System.out.print(arr[i]+" ");\par
       \}\par
       System.out.println();\par
   \}\par
\par
\par
   public static void main(String args[]) \{\par
       int arr[] = \{7, 8, 1, 3, 2\};\par
\par
\par
       //insertion sort\par
       for(int i=1; i<arr.length; i++) \{\par
           int current = arr[i];\par
           int j = i - 1;\par
               while(j >= 0 && arr[j] > current) \{\par
                   //Keep swapping\par
                   arr[j+1] = arr[j];\par
                   j--;\par
               \}\par
           arr[j+1] = current;\par
       \}\par
       printArray(arr);\par
   \}\par
\}\par
