\fs24 Access modifiers in java\par
\par
\b0\fs22 In Java, access modifiers control the visibility (who can access) of classes, variables (fields), methods, and constructors. They are an important part of encapsulation in Object-Oriented Programming.\par
\par
There are 4 access modifiers in Java:\par
\par
Class --> public , default but Inner Classes we can use all the 4\par
Methods --> we acn use all the modifiers\par
Variables (Instance & Static Fields) --> all the modifiers\par
Constructors --> --> we acn use all the modifiers\par
Interfaces --> Top-level interface  -->Only public or default\par
Members inside interface:\par
\par
Variables \f1\u8594? always public static final (by default)\par
Methods \u8594? always public\par
(Java 8+) can also have private methods inside interfaces\f0\lang1033\par
\par
\b 1. private\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Accessible only within the same class\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Not visible outside the class\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b 2. default (no modifier)\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Accessible within the same package\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Not accessible outside the package\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b 3. protected\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Within the same package \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Outside the package only through inheritance \par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
