Final Key Word \par
\b0 In Java, final is a keyword used to make something constant or restricted from changing.\par
It can be used with:\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Variable --> A final variable value cannot be changed once assigned.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Method --> A final method cannot be overridden by child classes.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Class --> A final class cannot be inherited.\b\par

