\b\fs24 Inheritance in Java\b0\fs22\par
Inheritance is a concept in Java where one class acquires the properties and behaviors (variables and methods) of another class.\par
\par
\b Why use Inheritance?\b0\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Reuse existing code\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Avoid duplicate code\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Improve maintainability\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Create logical relationship (is-a relationship)\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b Types of Inheritance in Java\par
\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj  Single Inheritance  --> \b0 One child, one parent\line class A \{\}\line class B extends A \{\}\line\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab} \b Multilevel Inheritance --> \b0 Chain of inheritance\line class A \{\}\line class B extends A \{\}\line class C extends B \{\}\line\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab} \b Hierarchical Inheritance --> \b0 One parent, multiple children\line class A \{\}\line class B extends A \{\}\line class C extends A \{\}\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}\b Multiple Inheritance  --> \b0 One child Multiple parents . Java does NOT support multiple inheritance using classes (to avoid confusion) , But supports using interfaces\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj           \par
\cf2\b IS-A represents inheritance using extends, while HAS-A represents composition where one class contains another class object.\cf0\par
\b0\par
\par
\b\fs24 1)Encapsulation\b0\fs22\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Encapsulation is the process of wrapping data (variables) and code (methods) together into a single unit (class) and restricting direct access to the data.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Access to data is restricted using access modifiers (private, public, protected).\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Provides data hiding.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Example: Using getters and setters to access private variables.\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b Why Encapsulation?\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Protects data from unauthorized access\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Provides data hiding\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Improves security and control\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Makes code easier to maintain\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b How to Achieve Encapsulation?\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b0 Declare variables as private\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Provide public getter and setter methods to access and update them\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\par
\b 2).Inheritance\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Mechanism where one class (child/subclass) inherits the properties and behaviors (fields and methods) of another class (parent/superclass).\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Promotes code reusability.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Syntax: class ChildClass extends ParentClass \{ \}\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b\fs24 Polymorphism\b0\fs22\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Ability of an object to take many forms(Polymorphism allows one method or object to perform different behaviors based on context.).\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b Compile-time polymorphismor static polymorphism (Method Overloading): \b0 Method Overloading is a concept in Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) where multiple methods in the same class have the same name but different parameters (different type, number, or order of parameters).\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b Run-time polymorphism (Method Overriding): \b0 Child class provides a specific implementation of a method already defined in parent class.\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b Dynamic Method Dispatch. -->\b0 Method call is decided at runtime based on the actual object, not the reference type.It is mainly used in runtime polymorphism.\b\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Method name must be same\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Parameters must be same (same signature)\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Return type must be same (or covariant)\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Access modifier cannot be reduced\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Example: public \f1\u8594? private \f0\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Only inherited methods can be overridden\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Cannot override static methods\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}\lang1033 Cannot override final methods\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Constructor cannot be overridden\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b\par
Abstraction \par
\par
\b0 Abstraction is a fundamental concept in programming (especially in Object-Oriented Programming \f2\endash\f0  OOP) that means hiding unnecessary details and showing only the important features of an object or system.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Hiding internal details and showing only the essential features.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Achieved using abstract classes and interfaces in Java.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Focuses on what an object does rather than how it does it.\b\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b0\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b Abstract Class --> \b0 A class declared with abstract keyword.\b\line\b0 Cannot create object directly\b\line\b0 Can contain:\line       1.normal methods\line       2.abstract methods\line       3.constructors\line       4.variables\line\b\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}Abstract Method  --> \b0 Method without body.Only declaration, no implementation.\b\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b0             abstract void sound();\par
\b\par
Rules of Abstract\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b0 If class has abstract method, class must be abstract.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Abstract class cannot be instantiated\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Child class must implement abstract Methods otherwise child class also becomes abstract.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Abstract class can have constructors.-->  used to initialize common properties when a subclass object is created.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Abstract methods cannot be: final.static and private. Because overriding is required.\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b Interface in Java\b0\par
An interface in Java is a blueprint of a class that contains only abstract methods (until Java 7) and defines what a class should do, but not how.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj  It is used to achieve 100% abstraction and multiple inheritance.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab} Methods are abstract by default\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Variables are public, static, and final (constants)\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Cannot create object of interface \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Class must implement all methods of interface\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Interface has no constructor\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}A class uses implements, not extends\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b\fs24 Types of Interfaces in Java\fs22\par
\b0 Java mainly has 4 types of interfaces:\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Normal Interface --> it can have Many abstract methods ,Default methods,Static methods,Constants\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Functional Interface --> it has only ONE abstract method.used in lambda expressions \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Marker Interface --> it has Zero methods. Only used to mark / tag a class. EX Serializable,Cloneable,RandomAccess.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}SAM (Single Abstract Method) Interface \f2\endash\f0  similar to functional (but defined separately in interviews)\b\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
Typecasting in Java\par
\b0 Converting one data type into another data type.\par
\par
There are 2 main types:\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b Primitive Type Casting  \b0 --> Converting primitive data types.\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Widening Casting (Implicit)  ->  Small datatype \f1\u8594? Bigger datatype\f0\lang1033\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Narrowing Casting (Explicit)  ->  Bigger datatype \f1\u8594? Smaller datatype\f0\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b Object Type Casting  \b0 --> Used with inheritance.\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Upcasting     -> Child object \f1\u8594? Parent reference\f0\lang1033 .\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Downcasting -> Parent reference \f1\u8594? Child reference\f0\lang1033   \par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b Wrapper class in Java\b0\par
Converting primitive data types into objects.\par
\par
