\par
There are 3 Main Types of Errors in Java\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\cf2\b0 Compile\f2\_\f0 Time Errors  \cf0\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj             These errors happen when you compile the code (before running).\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Syntax\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Missing semicolon\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Wrong keywords\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Wrong data types\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Misspelled classes/methods\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\cf2 Run\f2\_\f0 Time Errors\cf0\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj             These happen while the program is running, even if code compiled successfully.\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Dividing by zero\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}NullPointerException\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Array index out of bounds\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}File not found\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Input mismatch\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\cf2       Exception in Java\par
\cf0 An exception is an unexpected event that happens during program execution and disrupts the normal flow of the program.\par
\par
Types of Exceptions\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\cf2 Checked Exceptions \cf0 --> Checked by compiler,Must be handled using try-catch or throws Ex: IOException, SqlException & FileNotFoundException\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}\cf2 Un-Checked Exceptions \cf0 --> Occur at runtime,Caused by logic errors Ex:ArithmeticException,NullPointerException & ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsExceptio\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\b\par
How to Handle Exceptions?\par
\b0 A try\f2\endash\f0 catch block is used to handle exceptions in Java\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj try \f1\u8594? write risky code\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}catch \u8594? write handling code\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}finally \u8594? always runs\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Multiple catches \u8594? allowed\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}try cannot exist alone\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}catch must match exception type\f0\lang1033\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\f2\par
\b finally block?\b0\par
The finally block is used in exception handling and it always executes whether an exception occurs or not.\f0\par
\par
try \{\par
    // risky code\par
\} \par
catch (Exception e) \{\par
    // handle exception\par
\}\par
finally \{\par
    // always executes\par
\}\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj finally \f1\u8594? always executes\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Used for \u8594? cleanup tasks\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Runs \u8594? whether exception occurs or not\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Runs \u8594? even with return\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}May not run \u8594? only in rare cases (like system exit)\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
