\b Threads In java?\b0\par
A thread in Java is the smallest unit of execution within a program. It allows a program to perform multiple tasks simultaneously (this is called multithreading).\par
\par
A thread is a lightweight process that allows parallel execution of tasks within a program.\par
\par
