What is Synchronization in Java?\par
\b0 Synchronization is a process that controls the access of multiple threads to shared resources.\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\fi-360\li720\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Synchronization controls thread access to shared data\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}Prevents race conditions and data errors\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}Achieved using synchronized keyword\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
Types:\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\fi-360\li720\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj Method l\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}Block\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}Static\b\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
\b0 class Counter \{\par
    int count = 0;\par
\par
    synchronized void increment() \{\par
        count++;\par
    \}\par
\}\b\par
\par
What is join() in Java Thread?\par
\b0 join() is a method used to make one thread wait until another thread finishes execution.\par
\par
