\b What is Collections Class?\par
\b0 In Java, the Collections class is a utility class in the java.util package that provides static methods to perform common operations on collection objects (like List, Set, etc.).\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj It is not an interface, but a final class\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Contains only static methods\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Used to manipulate collections (sorting, searching, reversing, etc.)\b\par

\pard\ri-874\sl240\slmult1\qj\par
1. Sorting   -->\par
 \b0 Collections.sort(list); // ascending  order\par
 Collections.sort(list,Collections.reverseOrder()); // descending order\par
\b 2. Reverse --> \b0 Collections.reverse(list);\par
\b 3. Shuffle (Random order) -> \b0 Collections.shuffle(list);\par
\b 4. Minimum & Maximum ->\par
 \b0 int min = Collections.min(list); \par
int max = Collections.max(list);\par
\par
\b 5. Binary Search\b0 (Works only on sorted list)\b  ->\par
\b0 Collections.sort(list);\par
int index = Collections.binarySearch(list, 20);\par
\par
\b 6. Frequency (count occurrences)\b0  -> \par
List<String> names = Arrays.asList("A", "B", "A", "C", "A");\par
int count = Collections.frequency(names, "A");\par
\par
\b 7. Unmodifiable Collection \b0 (Cannot modify this list (read-only)) ->\par
List<Integer> unmodifiableList = Collections.unmodifiableList(list);\par
\par
\b 8.Synchronized Collection( Makes collection thread-safe) ->\b0\par
List<Integer> syncList = Collections.synchronizedList(list);\par
